  "content": "Election Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\nOnlinekhabar\nWednesday, October 8, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 8\nThe\nElection Commission\nhas called a meeting of political parties to discuss the House of Representatives election scheduled for March 5.\nBoth the government and the Election Commission had faced criticism for not consulting political parties before announcing the election date and publishing the schedule.\nFollowing the criticism for excluding parties participating in the election, the Election Commission has invited them for a discussion on October 16.\nElection Commission spokesperson Narayan Prasad Bhattarai said, “Preparations have been made to hold discussions with the parties on October 16. The formal invitation letter is yet to be sent.”\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nNepal\nElection Commission\ncricket\nshare market\nroad\nGen Z\nMaitighar\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nBy-polls: Code of conduct in effect from today\n1 year ago\nBy-election for Ilam 2 scheduled for April 27\n2 years ago\nCode of conduct for NA Election to come into effect from tomorrow\n2 years ago\nNational Assembly candidates can spend up to Rs 350,000 as election expense\n2 years ago\n52 set sights on 19 National Assembly seats\n2 years ago\nNational Assembly election: 549 voters from province assemblies, 1,498 from local levels\n2 years ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n3 hours ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n4 hours ago\nBlog\nHow Gen Z turned a hashtag into a revolution in Nepal\n4 hours ago\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n20 hours ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n21 hours ago",
